    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Kyle Tucker** (81.27), who remains our strongest play despite his lineup status currently being pending. Facing Me. Kelly, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and favorable park factors, cementing him as the core of our daily offensive output. He is closely shadowed by **Andy Pages** (73.64), whose move to the #2 spot creates a high-ceiling environment against a weak starter. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.22) anchors the middle infield with a robust 14% dynamic platoon edge against Mahle, the overall efficiency of the lineup is bolstered by **Jackson Merrill** (68.30) and **Gunnar Henderson** (63.19); although **Gunnar Henderson** faces an elite arm in Eovaldi, his elite speed and leadoff placement insulate his value in our pursuit of stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Liam Hicks**, who finished just outside the starting threshold at 39.67. While he carries promise, his match-up against Logan Gilbert\u2014a high-strikeout arm\u2014tipped the optimizer toward maintaining our floor elsewhere, particularly in favor of **Nasim Nunez** (63.70), who holds significant utility due to his 19% SP skill advantage against Petty. We are also monitoring a 40% rain risk hovering over **Jorge Polanco** (49.79), whose score is already marginalized by an unfavorable #8 spot in the order. Should the weather turn, we will pivot to ensure we are not wasting game caps on a dampened environment. Conversely, **Drake Baldwin** (58.11) and **Jacob Wilson** (57.74) remain solid, if unspectacular, plays, provided they navigate the challenges of Fried and Tolle respectively. We continue to hold **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** in reserve as we strategically manage our remaining game caps for the stretch run."